course: dictionary
lesson: 626
title: Babyhood and the stages of life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Babyhood is the time in your life when you are a baby, usually the first year or two. Other words name the stages that come next: childhood, adolescence (the teenage years), adulthood and old age. You will meet these words in science lessons about the human life cycle.
explain: Look at the words around babyhood for clues. «Most mammals stop digesting milk after babyhood» tells you that babyhood is a stage that ends, and that the body changes once it is over. The word after shows the order of the stages.
explain: Stories use babyhood in another way. When Grandma finds your old rattle, she is remembering your babyhood. Here the word brings back memories and feelings of long ago, not a science fact.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Most mammals stop digesting milk after the first year or two of life» still makes sense, so babyhood must mean that early time.
fact: Babyhood means the time in your life when you are a baby, usually the first year or two.
fact: The human life cycle has five stages: babyhood, childhood, adolescence, adulthood and old age.
fact: «Most mammals stop digesting milk after babyhood» means that for most mammals, the body stops digesting milk once the baby stage is over.
fact: «Lactose intolerant» describes grown-ups whose tummies get upset by milk, because they do not have the change that keeps milk digestion going.
fact: Babyhood is an uncountable noun, so you say «her babyhood», not «a babyhood».
exercise: What does babyhood mean? | *The time in your life when you are a baby, usually the first year or two | The time when you are old and retired | A toy you play with as a baby | The teenage years, when you are at secondary school
exercise: In the life cycle, which stage comes straight after babyhood? | Adolescence | *Childhood | Adulthood | Old age
exercise: Grandma found your old rattle from your babyhood. What does this tell you? | It was bought last week | It was from when you were a teenager | *It was from when you were a baby | It is a stone from the garden
test: Which stage of life comes straight after adolescence? | Old, meaning the time when you are 9 | Childhood | *Adulthood | Babyhood | 
test: What does «lactose intolerant» describe? | Babies who have never tasted milk | People who are always hungry | Animals that can run very fast | *Grown-ups who get tummy trouble from drinking milk
exam: Which sentence uses babyhood correctly? | *Her babyhood photos show her in a pram, smiling at the camera | His babyhood lasts until he is forty years old | Babyhood is the name of a football team | My grandad was a teenager during his babyhood
